title: 'Registrar: Force Register'

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |-
      Implements `pallet-registrar-para::force_register`, the port of the relay chain's
      `paras_registrar::force_register`, gated by the new `ForceOrigin` config type.

      Any id works, the system range included, and it need not be reserved first. The manager
      pays the usual deposits, as with `reserve` + `register`, unless the id is a system one or
      `skip_deposit` is set. That replaces the old `deposit` override, which Polkadot set to 0 for
      system chains. Deposit tickets in `ParaInfo` and `RegistrationState` are now `Option`s.
      `NextFreeParaId` moves past a forced public id so `reserve` doesn't collide with it.
      A forced system id the relay chain turns down, or whose registration is cancelled, is
      dropped rather than left reserved, and `register` refuses system ids with the new
      `SystemParaId` error, so only `force_register` picks a system para's code.
      New try-state checks fail on a reserved system id or a system para holding a deposit, and
      warn on a public para missing one.
      The call sends the existing `Register` message, so the relay chain side is unchanged. It
      comes with a new `force_register` weight.

crates:
  - name: pallet-registrar-para
    bump: major
